            <ArticleTitle>To Give Epinephrine or Not to Give Epinephrine-That Is (No Longer) The Question!</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>162-164</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1942602X17690402</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is vital that school nurses be able to assess students who are at risk for anaphylaxis and that nurses train school staff to identify the symptoms of a life-threatening allergic reaction. When a reaction occurs, school nurses and staff must be prepared to administer epinephrine immediately.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
